{"title":"SHAP  (**SH**apley **A**dditive ex**P**lanations)","markdown":{"headingText":"SHAP  (**SH**apley **A**dditive ex**P**lanations)","headingAttr":{"id":"","classes":["unnumbered"],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\nUse **SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)** values with **virtually any classification algorithm**.\n\nSHAP is model-agnostic, meaning it doesn't depend on the inner workings of a specific algorithm; instead, it works by evaluating how changing the inputs affects the model's output.\n\nHere are the most common classification algorithms grouped by type where SHAP is widely used:\n\n## Tree-Based Ensembles (Most Common)\n\nTree models are where SHAP is used most frequently because SHAP has a specialized, ultra-fast explainer algorithm for them (`TreeExplainer`).\n\n* **Random Forest Classifier**\n* **XGBoost Classifier** (`XGBClassifier`)\n* **LightGBM Classifier** (`LGBMClassifier`)\n* **CatBoost Classifier** (`CatBoostClassifier`)\n* **Decision Tree Classifier**\n\n## Linear & Generalized Linear Models\n\nFor linear models, SHAP helps one interpret the coefficients in an intuitive, game-theoretic way (`LinearExplainer`).\n\n* **Logistic Regression**\n* **Ridge Classifier**\n* **Linear Support Vector Classification (Linear SVC)**\n* **Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) Classifier**\n\n## Distance & Kernel-Based Models\n\nThese models don't have built-in tree structures or simple linear equations, so SHAP uses a slower, model-agnostic sampling approach (`KernelExplainer`) to approximate the values.\n\n* **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) Classifier**\n* **Support Vector Machine (SVM) with RBF/Non-linear Kernel**\n\n## Neural Networks / Deep Learning\n\nFor neural networks, SHAP can analyze activations and gradients to explain deep architectures (`DeepExplainer`).\n\n* **Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) Classifier** (Standard Deep Neural Networks)\n* **Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)** (Often used for image classification, like glaucoma fundus scans)\n\n## A Note on PyCaret Integration\n\nIf one is using **PyCaret**, PyCaret’s `interpret_model()` automatically detects the underlying machine learning algorithm selected via `compare_models()` and applies the correct SHAP explainer behind the scenes, whether it's handling a LightGBM model, a Random Forest, or Logistic Regression!","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","reference-location":"margin","output-file":"shapley.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-prefix":"Source","other-links-t